{"lessons":[{"subject":"sci","level":"b8","topic":"5.3 Science and Industry","kind":"learn","title":"Science, Technology, Innovation and Society","emoji":"🌟","order":1,"status":"published","pages":[{"title":"What you will learn","body":"🎯 **By the end of this lesson you will be able to:**\n- Explain the interrelationship of science, technology and innovation.\n- Discuss technological advancements in the world and their impact on the Ghanaian environment."},{"title":"Defining Science, Technology and Innovation","body":"Science, technology and innovation are three closely related but distinct ideas that together shape how societies develop and solve problems. Science is the systematic study of the natural world through observation and experimentation, aimed at understanding how things work. Technology is the practical application of scientific knowledge to create tools, devices or systems that solve real problems. Innovation is the process of developing new ideas, methods or products, often by creatively applying science and technology in new ways."}],"questions":[{"t":"mcq","q":"Science is best described as","o":["The practical application of tools to solve problems only","The process of adopting new ideas without study","The study of society only","The systematic study of the natural world through observation and experimentation"],"c":3,"e":"Science is the systematic study of the natural world through observation and experimentation, aimed at understanding how things work."},{"t":"mcq","q":"Technology is best described as","o":["A random guess with no scientific basis","The practical application of scientific knowledge to solve problems","The study of the natural world only","The study of the past only"],"c":1,"e":"Technology is the practical application of scientific knowledge to create tools, devices or systems that solve real problems."},{"t":"mcq","q":"Innovation is best described as","o":["Copying old ideas exactly with no change","Ignoring science and technology completely","The process of developing new ideas, methods or products","The study of natural phenomena only"],"c":2,"e":"Innovation is the process of developing new ideas, methods or products, often by creatively applying science and technology in new ways."}],"source":"B8_5.1_to_5.6_Humans_and_the_Environment.docx","id":"b8-5.3-01"},{"subject":"sci","level":"b8","topic":"5.3 Science and Industry","kind":"learn","title":"How Science, Technology, Innovation and Society Connect","emoji":"🔬","order":2,"status":"published","pages":[{"title":"How Science, Technology, Innovation and Society Connect","body":"Scientific discovery, technological application, societal need, and environmental impact are four interconnected elements that influence one another continuously, rather than functioning in a simple, one directional chain.\n\n- Science often begins with curiosity or a societal need, such as understanding why crops fail, which leads to new scientific knowledge, such as understanding soil nutrients.\n\n- Technology takes this scientific knowledge and turns it into practical tools, such as improved fertilisers or irrigation systems.\n\n- Innovation may then combine or adapt these technologies in creative new ways, such as designing low cost irrigation systems suited to smallholder farms.\n\n- Society adopts, adapts, or sometimes resists these innovations depending on cost, culture, and perceived benefit, while the environment is affected, positively or negatively, by how these technologies are used."},{"title":"Technological Advancements and Their Impact on Ghana","body":"Mobile phones, improved farming equipment, solar power, medical technology, and motor vehicles are examples of technological advancements that have had a significant impact, both positive and negative, on the Ghanaian environment and society, as summarised in the table below.\n\n| **TECHNOLOGICAL ADVANCEMENT** | **IMPACT ON THE GHANAIAN ENVIRONMENT AND SOCIETY** |\n|---|---|\n| **Mobile phones and the internet** | Improved communication and access to information, but increased demand for electricity and electronic waste |\n| **Improved farming equipment and methods** | Increased crop yields and food security, but sometimes increased fuel use and land clearing |\n| **Solar power technology** | Provided electricity to remote communities without damaging emissions, reducing reliance on fuel wood |\n| **Improved medical technology** | Better diagnosis and treatment of diseases, extending and improving quality of life |\n| **Motor vehicles and transport technology** | Faster movement of people and goods, but increased air pollution and traffic congestion in cities |"}],"questions":[{"t":"mcq","q":"Mobile phones have impacted Ghanaian society mainly by","o":["Having no effect on communication at all","Improving communication and access to information","Reducing all forms of communication","Removing the need for electricity entirely"],"c":1,"e":""},{"t":"mcq","q":"Solar power technology has helped some Ghanaian communities mainly by","o":["Increasing reliance on fuel wood","Providing electricity without damaging emissions","Removing the need for any electricity","Requiring significant fuel wood burning"],"c":1,"e":""},{"t":"mcq","q":"Improved farming technology can increase crop yields but sometimes leads to","o":["Decreased food security","Increased fuel use and land clearing","No environmental impact at all","Reduced use of any land"],"c":1,"e":""},{"t":"mcq","q":"Motor vehicles and transport technology have contributed to","o":["Faster movement of goods and people, but increased pollution in cities","No environmental impact of any kind","Reduced movement of people and goods","Slower transportation only"],"c":0,"e":""}],"source":"B8_5.1_to_5.6_Humans_and_the_Environment.docx","id":"b8-5.3-02"},{"subject":"sci","level":"b8","topic":"5.3 Science and Industry","kind":"learn","title":"Science, Technology, Innovation and Society (part 3)","emoji":"🧪","order":3,"status":"published","pages":[{"title":"Look at the picture","body":"[[img:if65914e77|Fig 6.1  Science, technology, innovation, society and the environment as interconnected influences on one another]]\n\nNotice that the connections between these four areas run in multiple directions, not just one. Society's needs can drive new scientific research, scientific discoveries can enable new technologies, technologies can spark further innovation, and all of these can, in turn, affect the environment, which then influences future scientific questions and societal priorities."},{"title":"Going further","body":"> 💡 **Going further**\n\nUnderstanding the relationship among science, technology, innovation and society helps citizens make informed decisions about new developments, rather than simply accepting or rejecting them without consideration. For example, weighing the clear benefits of improved transport technology against its environmental costs, such as air pollution, can help guide better choices, such as investing in cleaner vehicle technology or improved public transport systems."}],"questions":[{"t":"mcq","q":"Which of the following best describes how science, technology and society interact?","o":["Society has no role in shaping technology at all","Technology never affects the environment","They influence each other in multiple directions, not just one","They operate in a strict, one directional line with no feedback"],"c":2,"e":"Notice that the connections between these four areas run in multiple directions, not just one."},{"t":"mcq","q":"Understanding the connections among science, technology, innovation and society mainly helps","o":["Citizens make informed decisions about new developments","Prevent all forms of technological change","Remove the need for scientific study","Society ignore environmental impacts completely"],"c":0,"e":"Understanding the relationship among science, technology, innovation and society helps citizens make informed decisions about new developments, rather than simply accepting or rejecting them without consideration."},{"t":"mcq","q":"Weighing the benefits of transport technology against its environmental costs is an example of","o":["Ignoring all technology completely","Informed decision making about technology and its impact","Rejecting all forms of transport","Removing science from society"],"c":1,"e":"Understanding the relationship among science, technology, innovation and society helps citizens make informed decisions about new developments, rather than simply accepting or rejecting them without consideration."}],"source":"B8_5.1_to_5.6_Humans_and_the_Environment.docx","id":"b8-5.3-03"},{"subject":"sci","level":"b8","topic":"5.3 Science and Industry","kind":"test","title":"Topic test","emoji":"🏆","order":900,"status":"published","pages":[],"questions":[{"t":"mcq","q":"Science is best described as","o":["The practical application of tools to solve problems only","The process of adopting new ideas without study","The study of society only","The systematic study of the natural world through observation and experimentation"],"c":3,"e":"Science is the systematic study of the natural world through observation and experimentation, aimed at understanding how things work."},{"t":"mcq","q":"Technology is best described as","o":["A random guess with no scientific basis","The practical application of scientific knowledge to solve problems","The study of the natural world only","The study of the past only"],"c":1,"e":"Technology is the practical application of scientific knowledge to create tools, devices or systems that solve real problems."},{"t":"mcq","q":"Innovation is best described as","o":["Copying old ideas exactly with no change","Ignoring science and technology completely","The process of developing new ideas, methods or products","The study of natural phenomena only"],"c":2,"e":"Innovation is the process of developing new ideas, methods or products, often by creatively applying science and technology in new ways."},{"t":"mcq","q":"Mobile phones have impacted Ghanaian society mainly by","o":["Having no effect on communication at all","Improving communication and access to information","Reducing all forms of communication","Removing the need for electricity entirely"],"c":1,"e":""},{"t":"mcq","q":"Solar power technology has helped some Ghanaian communities mainly by","o":["Increasing reliance on fuel wood","Providing electricity without damaging emissions","Removing the need for any electricity","Requiring significant fuel wood burning"],"c":1,"e":""},{"t":"mcq","q":"Improved farming technology can increase crop yields but sometimes leads to","o":["Decreased food security","Increased fuel use and land clearing","No environmental impact at all","Reduced use of any land"],"c":1,"e":""},{"t":"mcq","q":"Motor vehicles and transport technology have contributed to","o":["Faster movement of goods and people, but increased pollution in cities","No environmental impact of any kind","Reduced movement of people and goods","Slower transportation only"],"c":0,"e":""},{"t":"mcq","q":"Which of the following best describes how science, technology and society interact?","o":["Society has no role in shaping technology at all","Technology never affects the environment","They influence each other in multiple directions, not just one","They operate in a strict, one directional line with no feedback"],"c":2,"e":"Notice that the connections between these four areas run in multiple directions, not just one."},{"t":"mcq","q":"Understanding the connections among science, technology, innovation and society mainly helps","o":["Citizens make informed decisions about new developments","Prevent all forms of technological change","Remove the need for scientific study","Society ignore environmental impacts completely"],"c":0,"e":"Understanding the relationship among science, technology, innovation and society helps citizens make informed decisions about new developments, rather than simply accepting or rejecting them without consideration."},{"t":"mcq","q":"Weighing the benefits of transport technology against its environmental costs is an example of","o":["Ignoring all technology completely","Informed decision making about technology and its impact","Rejecting all forms of transport","Removing science from society"],"c":1,"e":"Understanding the relationship among science, technology, innovation and society helps citizens make informed decisions about new developments, rather than simply accepting or rejecting them without consideration."}],"source":"B8_5.1_to_5.6_Humans_and_the_Environment.docx","id":"b8-5.3-04"}],"images":[{"id":"if65914e77","d":"data:image/jpeg;base64,"}]}